<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaji' Imox</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1540</span> · Also known as Cahi Imox</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaji' Imox was one of the two kings of the Kaqchikel Maya at Iximche in highland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beleheb-kat">Beleheb' Kat</a> he welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-alvarado">Pedro de Alvarado</a> in 1524 and allied with the Spanish against the K'iche'. Harsh Spanish demands provoked a Kaqchikel revolt that lasted until 1530, and he was later hanged by Alvarado in 1540.</p></div>
